{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"STRUCTURAL COST OBSERVED (worth recording for the epic): landing a consolidation change INVALIDATES its own ticket's plan-review attestation, because the review pins the code and the change modifies exactly the files the plan names. 4329's close-review came back 'stale-code: 4 dependency file(s) changed' naming the very files it landed. So each leaf needs a SECOND full plan review after merge purely to satisfy the close gate - roughly doubling LLM spend per leaf. This compounds with bug a83f (the sign fence), because that second review must not only PASS but persist a signature against a tracker that is rarely quiet. Throughput on this epic is now gated by the review/attestation cycle, not by the coding: the three leaves implemented so far each took one implementer pass and first-attempt-green happy paths, while their plans took 2-4 review rounds apiece."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787375105262753001,"uuid":"383f8831-2d7d-44c1-b2d4-0fb9a879c5ff"}